<title>GREECE: ALPHA CREDIT BANK HOLDS PRIME RATE AT 17.25 PCT.</title>
<headline>ALPHA CREDIT BANK HOLDS PRIME RATE AT 17.25 PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Alpha Credit Bank will keep its prime rate for working capital and fixed asset loans unchanged at 17.25 percent, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Alpha Credit, which reviews its rates weekly, said the maximum add-on would remain unchanged at 3.5 percent.</p>
<p>Its adjustable-rate mortgages are set at 17.50 percent. The bank launched 15-year mortgages in October 1995 with rates set at 12.0 percent for the first five years.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
